@widths 5.8,3.6,4.6
@font 9.5
Indicator | Figure | Source (year)
Population; growth rate | about 241 million; 2.55% a year | Census (2023)
Literacy — overall; men; women | 60.65%; about 68%; about 53% | Census (2023)
Female literacy "as stated in the paper" | 48% | MCQ 2019
Out-of-school children | more than 25 million, most of them girls | —
Female labour-force participation ★ | 24.4% (21.4% in 2020–21) | LFS (2024–25)
Provincial female LFPR ★ | Punjab 33.8%; KP 21.1%; Sindh 20.5%; Balochistan 14.5% | LFS (2024–25)
Male labour-force participation | roughly 80% | LFS (2024–25)
Unpaid care work | women do about 3 times men's unpaid care (worldwide) | ILO (2018)
Maternal mortality ratio | 186 per 100,000 live births | PMMS (2019)
Anaemia among women aged 15–49 | about 42% | NNS (2018)
Stunting among children under five | about 40% | NNS (2018)
Total fertility rate; contraceptive use | about 3.6; about 34% | PDHS (2017–18)
Skilled birth attendance | about two-thirds of births | PDHS (2017–18)
Public spending | health about 1% of GDP; education about 2% | —
Breast cancer deaths "as stated in the paper" | about 13,000 a year | MCQ 2019
Pregnant women in 2022 flood areas | about 650,000 | UNFPA (2022)
People affected by the 2022 floods | about 33 million | Government / UN (2022)
Transgender persons counted | 10,418 | Census (2017)
