@widths 5.8,3.6,4.6
@font 9.5
Indicator | Figure | Source (year)
Women worldwide experiencing physical or sexual violence | about 1 in 3 (≈736 million) | WHO (2021); MCQ 2024
Women and girls killed intentionally worldwide | about 85,000 | UNODC / UN Women (2023)
Killed by partners or family | about 51,100 — one every 10 minutes | UNODC / UN Women (2023)
Ever-married women: physical violence since 15 | 28% | PDHS (2017–18)
Ever-married women: sexual violence | 6% | PDHS (2017–18)
Spousal physical, sexual or emotional violence | 34% | PDHS (2017–18)
Survivors who never sought help | 56% | PDHS (2017–18)
Reported GBV cases ★ | 32,617 | SSDO (2024)
Rape / kidnapping / domestic violence / honour cases ★ | 5,339 / 24,439 / 2,238 / 547 | SSDO (2024)
Conviction rates ★ | rape 0.5%; honour 0.5%; DV 1.3%; kidnapping 0.1% | SSDO (2024)
Honour killings ★ | at least 405 | HRCP (2024)
Honour killings (latest) ★ | at least 470; 1,332 domestic-violence murders; 2,586 cyber-harassment cases | HRCP (2025; report May 2026)
Cost of violence against women | about 2% of world GDP | UN Women estimate
:::

