## 3.6  South Asia at a glance

::: table | Women in South Asian parliaments (latest elections).
@widths 2.6,4.4,3.4,3.6
@font 9.5
Country | National quota | Women in lower house | Source (year)
Pakistan | 60 reserved seats; 5% tickets | about one-fifth | 2024
India | One-third after delimitation (2023 Act) | 74 (about 14%) | 2024
Bangladesh | 50 reserved seats | 57 of 350 (7 directly elected) | 2026
Sri Lanka | No national quota; 25% local | 22 of 225 | 2024
Nepal | One-third by constitution (2015) | 96 of 275 (14 via FPTP) | 2026
:::

::: trap | Five numbers candidates mix up
1. **60 seats, 17%, 33%** — 60 reserved NA seats (since 2002) are about **17%** of 342; **33%** was the **local** quota of 2000–01.
2. **405 and 470** — HRCP's honour-killing counts for **2024** and **2025**; SSDO's **547** (2024) counts reported cases differently.
3. **25% and 8%** — the mobile-internet gap was 25% in 2024 (the exam note's figure) and 8% in 2025.
4. **143/144 and 143/145** — "second-worst" was **2017** (of 144); **2026** is 143rd of **145**.
5. **28% and 34%** — PDHS: **28%** physical violence since 15; **34%** any spousal violence (physical, sexual or emotional).
:::
